The attached image is a Western blot (Figure 7D from the 2015 PDF) demonstrating the processing and secretion of IL-1β by dendritic cells under various stimulation conditions. It shows that inactive pro-IL-1β (∼30kD) is present in cell lysates, particularly when cells are primed with LPS. Active, secreted IL-1β (∼17kD) is detected in the supernatant, with a strong increase observed when dendritic cells are stimulated with Nano-11, especially in combination with LPS priming. This confirms that Nano-11 induces the cleavage and release of the active form of IL-1β, a crucial pro-inflammatory cytokine for immune response, which ELISA alone could not distinguish from the inactive form.